<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ie545e6d93db114cdba6a0652c6edb0b9d41cb977" commit="e60df7f73297dbcf26168e83fb143fc775edd47b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: Renormalize config  Run &quot;chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig oldconfig&quot; and accept all defaults.  CONFIG_DRM_POWERVR_ROGUE* due to: e9001eb10727 CHROMIUM: Mark DRM_POWERVR_ROGUE[_1_7] as BROKEN  CONFIG_VIRTIO_WL due to: ee3ae46ee497 virtwl: add virtwl driver  BUG=none TEST=Built and boot  Change-Id: Ie545e6d93db114cdba6a0652c6edb0b9d41cb977 Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/643032 Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="643032" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/32/643032/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I8843ae26cc7a5f1e0a5811cab2a9e9e34f78cc80" commit="a32bbb18380192111f36b7d2acd3c68b0b41f715" commit_message="FROMGIT: ASoC: rockchip: Remove unnecessary function call  First of all,the address of pdev-&gt;dev is assigned to card-&gt;dev,then the function platform_set_drvdata copies the value the variable card to pdev-&gt;dev.driver_data, but when calling snd_soc_register_card,the function dev_set_drvdata(card-&gt;dev, card) will also do the same copy operation,so i think that the former copy operation can be removed.  Signed-off-by: Peng Donglin &lt;dolinux.peng@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from git.kernel.org broonie/sound for-next  commit dc94d245a57b76f38c7a936cf900cc38237638de)  Conflicts:  sound/soc/rockchip/rk3288_hdmi_analog.c  BUG=b:64034515 TEST=build and boot  Change-Id: I8843ae26cc7a5f1e0a5811cab2a9e9e34f78cc80 Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/643034 Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="643034" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/34/643034/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I1fea85042760940dbbe70152882b9472a776452a" commit="9a590c23a56f3e0a219310360d79dd2a95506b9c" commit_message="FROMGIT: ASoC: rockchip: constify snd_soc_ops structures  Check for snd_soc_ops structures that are only stored in the ops field of a snd_soc_dai_link structure.  This field is declared const, so snd_soc_ops structures that have this property can be declared as const also.  The semantic patch that makes this change is as follows: (http://coccinelle.lip6.fr/)  // &lt;smpl&gt; @r disable optional_qualifier@ identifier i; position p; @@ static struct snd_soc_ops i@p = { ... };  @ok1@ identifier r.i; struct snd_soc_dai_link e; position p; @@ e.ops = &amp;i@p;  @ok2@ identifier r.i, e; position p; @@ struct snd_soc_dai_link e[] = { ..., { .ops = &amp;i@p, }, ..., };  @bad@ position p != {r.p,ok1.p,ok2.p}; identifier r.i; struct snd_soc_ops e; @@ e@i@p  @depends on !bad disable optional_qualifier@ identifier r.i; @@ static +const  struct snd_soc_ops i = { ... }; // &lt;/smpl&gt;  The effect on the layout of the .o files is shown by the following output of the size command, first before then after the transformation:     text    data     bss     dec     hex filename    5027    2488     416    7931    1efb sound/soc/rockchip/rk3399_gru_sound.o    5219    2312     416    7947    1f0b sound/soc/rockchip/rk3399_gru_sound.o     text    data     bss     dec     hex filename    3499    1648     384    5531    159b sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_max98090.o    3563    1584     384    5531    159b sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_max98090.o     text    data     bss     dec     hex filename    3455    1536     384    5375    14ff sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_rt5645.o    3519    1480     384    5383    1507 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_rt5645.o  Signed-off-by: Julia Lawall &lt;Julia.Lawall@lip6.fr&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from git.kernel.org broonie/sound for-next  commit 705e9994a437bbdaf655612f3526e3567db56bdd)  Conflicts:  sound/soc/rockchip/rk3399_gru_sound.c  sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_max98090.c  BUG=b:64034515 TEST=build and boot  Change-Id: I1fea85042760940dbbe70152882b9472a776452a Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/643033 Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="643033" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/643033/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I83f4fd4d7e045e074afb38c3d236bb31cd53e32e" commit="589f746fe7b43275f95b0897aeb5abb765aea659" commit_message="FROMGIT: ASoC: Add a sanity check before using dai driver name  The dai driver's name is allowed to be NULL. So add a sanity check for that.  Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reported-by: Donglin Peng &lt;dolinux.peng@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from git.kernel.org broonie/sound for-next  commit 6a6dafda937cfcdbbfe46a3e093de8bb929ba52d)  BUG=b:64034515 TEST=build and boot  Change-Id: I83f4fd4d7e045e074afb38c3d236bb31cd53e32e Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/643035 Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="643035" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/35/643035/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I0ad92e253d5ab8ae60e4c561fc24e6a8f6356eb4" commit="183023f730a1f559ec5c6ff0e01cbd6faf170ff3" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: Implementing airtime fairness based TX scheduler.  Ath10k driver/firmare has very deep(&gt;2000) transmit queues, this makes the fq_codel in mac80211 driver not effective at all, since the sojourn time measured in mac80211 is almost always below target.  Adding an airtime based transmit scheduler here to release just enough packets to keep hardware busy, while keep the rest of packets in mac80211 layer's queue, so fq_codel can have a better measurement of sojourn time and act properly upon it.  BUG=b:63994931 TEST=Wifi stress test.  Change-Id: I0ad92e253d5ab8ae60e4c561fc24e6a8f6356eb4 Signed-off-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/588190 Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="588190" owner_email="kyan@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="13" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/90/588190/13" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ia8afff4468f52c07ba07dbb447d2f296901af619" commit="e45f276d971fb4a4e3f8096a52a0082b1f198dcc" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: debugfs entry for airtime fairness scheduler.  BUG=b:63994931 TEST=Test read/write of new entrys in debugfs of ath10k.  Change-Id: Ia8afff4468f52c07ba07dbb447d2f296901af619 Signed-off-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/588191 Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="588191" owner_email="kyan@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/588191/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I4944761081b7f032fff071ae82de26c7bbaa8a36" commit="414c6a1d8fc5b12052bf44427504ee174e82b6dd" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: use frame count as deficit for fq_codel.  Applying fq_codel in mac80211 could cause imbalance for concurrent upstream/downstream traffic. When fq_codel applies only to downstream traffic and upstream traffic from client will dominates.  Use frame count instead of byte count as deficit for fq_codel, so a large data packet will be treat as the same a small TCP ACK packet.  BUG=b:63994931 TEST=wifi stress test.  Change-Id: I4944761081b7f032fff071ae82de26c7bbaa8a36 Signed-off-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/588192 Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="588192" owner_email="kyan@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/92/588192/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8bc49d2f0099065cb743f94ce3a8ff6d26c6ad96" commit="b8954942017f258c8ee4ab1f5622a2ac5893014e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mac80211: Improve aqm's debugfs entry  Make fq_codel's target and interval configurable through debugfs. Add fq_codel's stats in aqm's debugfs output.  BUG=b:63994931 TEST=&quot;echo fq_target 20000' &gt; /sys/kernel/debug/ieee80211/phy1/aqm&quot;  Change-Id: I8bc49d2f0099065cb743f94ce3a8ff6d26c6ad96 Signed-off-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/631189 Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="631189" owner_email="kyan@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/89/631189/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5908c2a61ba2d66c79948610e046f7aa62f84fb7" commit="3c065a587b105fc99150b0291c952995ddde7ad1" commit_message="shill: Add SetFixedIpParams() device setting  Allow callers to specify that an interface's IP parameters should not be changed.  This will be used for the ARC network bridge interface, which is not configured through shill.  When ARC becomes the default service, we want shill to change the systemwide DNS and routing configuration but we do not want it to manipulate the interface's IP configuration (address, prefix, broadcast, or interface up/down state).  BUG=chromium:696865 TEST=unit tests  Change-Id: I5908c2a61ba2d66c79948610e046f7aa62f84fb7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/573642 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="573642" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/42/573642/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2b648f93520ba7dc00ef171641e01607917e3a6c" commit="3b99b8e24ab37bae5647d55e0c70f0d1ef91862f" commit_message="shill: Allow --arc-device to be specified on command line  The ARC device is a network interface that connects the host system with an ARC container.  shill needs to know which interface it is so that it can set up ARC based VPNs.  The command line option allows the interface to be changed from the upstart scripts, which is where much of the other ARC network / bridge configuration takes place.  The IP configuration of the ARC device will not be managed by shill. Absent an ARC VPN, it will behave similarly to a blacklisted device.  By default this will use the interface name &quot;arcbr0&quot; instead of &quot;br0&quot;, and the cheets-scripts will be updated accordingly.  This way, a user who is not running ARC will not see surprising behavioral differences between a bridge named &quot;br0&quot; and a bridge named &quot;br1&quot;.  BUG=chromium:696865 TEST=use --arc-device=arcbr0 instead of adding it to the blacklist, and      verify that shill leaves its IP configuration alone  Change-Id: I2b648f93520ba7dc00ef171641e01607917e3a6c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/573643 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="573643" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/43/573643/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifa467f7b715bfce7e07de472b5bb8632ef8b3659" commit="d9da40821d5daee8935b185d9c5a9e2ee3cb414a" commit_message="shill: Add ArcVpnDriver  A service of type &quot;arcvpn&quot; modifies the system routing and DNS configuration so that Chrome browser traffic is sent through |StaticIP.Gateway| on ${ARC_DEVICE}.  BUG=chromium:696865 TEST=cd /usr/local/lib/flimflam/test &amp;&amp; \      ./configure-service arcvpn \         Name arcvpn \         Type vpn \         Provider.Type arcvpn \         Provider.Host arcvpn \         StaticIP.Gateway 100.115.92.2 \         StaticIP.NameServers 8.8.4.4 \         ArcVpn.TunnelChrome true &amp;&amp; \      ./connect-service arcvpn  Change-Id: Ifa467f7b715bfce7e07de472b5bb8632ef8b3659 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/573644 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="573644" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/44/573644/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I88777ee4fb47a3aca9283d55f3fab6f46fb3e4a0" commit="a0809e8d68344770148dd2e84f1ae1726f8127d3" commit_message="chromeos-base/arc-build-nyc: mutually exclusive with arc-build-master  BUG=b:65163422 TEST=Build packages and test image with the following use flags:    USE='android-container -android-container-nyc -android-container-master-arc-dev'   USE='-android-container android-container-nyc -android-container-master-arc-dev'   USE='-android-container -android-container-nyc android-container-master-arc-dev'  Change-Id: I88777ee4fb47a3aca9283d55f3fab6f46fb3e4a0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/624864 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="624864" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/64/624864/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3e4a625171b6661f16b192e234a707169128a9aa" commit="ff